msgstr "\n"
"=====================================\n"
"|icon| sequence_date_range 10.0.1.0.0\n"
"=====================================\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"**Module used to use the year of the date_to     into sequences (instead of date_from)**\n"
"\n"
".. |icon| image:: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zeroincombenze/server-tools/10.0/sequence_date_range/static/description/icon.png\n"
"\n"
"|Maturity| |Build Status| |Coverage Status| |Codecov Status| |license gpl| |Tech Doc| |Help| |Try Me|\n"
"\n"
".. contents::\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Overview / Panoramica\n"
"=====================\n"
"\n"
"|en| Currently, the range_year is the date filled into the date_from.\n"
"\n"
"This add-on allow the user to pick the date field used as the range_year\n"
"parameter into sequence generation.\n"
"\n"
"Ex: date_from = '2018-10-01' and date_to = '2019-09-30'.\n"
"If you select 'date_to' as reference date, your range_year will be 2019\n"
"(instead of 2018 if you let the default 'date_from').\n"
"\n"
"You can setup this field into sequences configuration.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"|\n"
"\n"
"|it| Descrizione in italiano non (ancora) disponibile\n"
"\n"
"|\n"
"\n"
